=== WHAT THIS PROVES (WMMA is safely additive) ===
The Todo 22 acceptance requires: "If WMMA correctness fails locally, it is excluded
from the tuning cache (correctness-gated) and the scalar baseline remains — never
blocks the wave." This log demonstrates exactly that. A WMMA fragment with a
DELIBERATELY WRONG lane-mapping produces a result that FAILS golden decisively, so the
autotuner would mark it validated=false and EXCLUDE it — while the UNCHANGED scalar
baseline (kernels/generated/matmul.cu, Todo 10) STILL PASSES on the identical inputs.
A bad WMMA variant can never replace the correct scalar baseline.

=== THE DELIBERATE BUG (a believable WMMA lane-mapping mistake) ===
matmul_wmma.cu's kernel is templated on BadLane. The CORRECT RDNA3 store lane-mapping
interleaves rows across the two lane halves:
    row = base_m + 2*e + (lane >> 4)        # even rows in lanes 0..15, odd in 16..31
The BadLane=true variant substitutes the BELIEVABLE BUG of assuming CONTIGUOUS rows per
half (the mistake a developer makes by guessing the layout instead of reading the
GPUOpen RDNA3 WMMA guide):
    row = base_m + 8*(lane >> 4) + e        # WRONG: scrambles the output rows
A and B fragment LOADING is identical (correct) in both; only the accumulator STORE
lane-mapping differs — isolating the bug to the output fragment layout, exactly "a
WMMA fragment with a wrong lane-mapping". The scrambled output fails all three golden
metrics (cosine/pcc collapse to ~0.15 for random data; max_rel_err explodes).

